.TH SPINCLASS-BUILD-PINS 7 "" "spinclass" "Spinclass Reference"
.SH NAME
spinclass-build-pins \- build-time-pinned binaries (madder, direnv, dodder)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Spinclass exposes a Nix flake function
.B lib.mkSpinclass
that produces a spinclass binary with absolute
.I /nix/store
paths burned in for selected runtime tools.
At link time these paths are written into package-level Go variables
via
.B \-X
.IR ldflags ,
and the binary picks them up at runtime without consulting
.BR PATH .
.PP
The default
.B packages.default
output of the spinclass flake is
.B mkSpinclass {}
\(em no inputs supplied, all pinned paths empty, every integration
dormant.
A consumer flake that wants the integrations active calls
.B mkSpinclass
with the desired derivations:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
spinclass.lib.${system}.mkSpinclass {
  madder = madder.packages.${system}.default;
  direnv = pkgs.direnv;
  dodder = dodder.packages.${system}.default;
}
.fi
.RE
.SH PINS
.SS madder
When the
.B madder
input is supplied,
.BR sc\ start " (and any other path that creates a worktree)"
initialises a per-worktree blob store at
.I <worktree>/.madder/local/share/blob_stores/default/
on first session creation.
The init command run is
.RS 4
.B madder init -encryption none .default
.RE
with
.B MADDER_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=<worktree>
set on the invocation only (not exported into the broader session) so
madder will not walk up into a parent repo's
.I .madder/
directory during store discovery.
.PP
The init step is guarded by an existence check on
.I blob_store-config
\(em rerunning
.B sc start
in a worktree that already has a store is a no-op.
.PP
When the integration is active, two additional rules are applied at
worktree creation:
.IP \(bu 2
.I .madder/
is appended to the worktree's
.IR .git/info/exclude .
.IP \(bu 2
.B Bash(madder:*)
is appended to the worktree's Claude Code allow list in
.IR .claude/settings.local.json .
.PP
When the
.B madder
input is null (the default
.BR packages.default ),
none of the above happens.
The feature is fully dormant; no
.I .madder/
directory is created and no madder-related allow rule is added.
.PP
When madder is pinned, the
.B sc merge
/
.B merge-this-session
and
.B sc check
/
.B check-this-session
flows emit a
.B compact response shape:
the pre-merge hook stage is a single verdict line in the plain
rendering of the ndjson-crap stream; on failure its diagnostic carries
.BR command ,
.BR exit_code ,
.BR elapsed ,
a 15-line
.B tail
of stdout+stderr, and a
.B resource_link
URI of the form
.B madder://blobs/<digest>
that points at the full hook output stored in the per-worktree blob
store (surfaced to MCP clients as a resource_link content block; it
only needs to be followed on failure).
Without madder pinned, no blob is stored and no resource_link is
emitted; the hook's lines still stream as live output records (the
viewport's rolling tail), and a failure falls back to the inline tail.
.SS direnv
When the
.B direnv
input is supplied, spinclass invokes the pinned binary directly
instead of consulting
.BR PATH .
When the input is null, spinclass falls back to
.BR exec.LookPath ;
if no
.B direnv
is found, the
.I .envrc
generation step is skipped (this matches the pre-pin behaviour).
.SS dodder
When the
.B dodder
input is supplied,
.BR sc\ start " (and any other path that creates a worktree)"
additionally initialises a per-worktree dodder repository at
.I <worktree>/.dodder/
on first session creation, layered over the per-worktree madder blob
store: when the madder
.B .default
store already exists it is adopted via
.BR "\-blob_store\-id .default" ;
otherwise dodder's embedded madder creates a default store.
The init command run is
.RS 4
.B dodder init -encryption none -repo_id . -private_key <key> [\-blob_store\-id .default] <repo-id>
.RE
with both
.B DODDER_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=<worktree>
and
.B MADDER_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=<worktree>
set on the invocation only (not exported into the broader session) so
discovery will not walk up into a parent repo's
.IR .dodder/ " or " .madder/
directories.
The signing key is resolved from the user's ssh agent via
.B dodder info-ssh_agent
(first key listed); a locked or empty agent is a hard error so no
divergent per-worktree signing identity is silently generated.
.PP
The init step is guarded by an existence check on
.I .dodder/local/share/config-seed
\(em rerunning
.B sc start
in a worktree that already has a repository is a no-op.
.PP
When the integration is active, two additional rules are applied at
worktree creation:
.IP \(bu 2
.I .dodder/
is appended to the worktree's
.IR .git/info/exclude .
.IP \(bu 2
.B Bash(dodder:*)
is appended to the worktree's Claude Code allow list in
.IR .claude/settings.local.json .
.PP
When the
.B dodder
input is null (the default
.BR packages.default ),
none of the above happens.
The feature is fully dormant; no
.I .dodder/
directory is created and no dodder-related allow rule is added.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spinclass (1),
.BR spinclass\-sweatfile (5),
.BR madder (1),
.BR direnv (1),
.BR dodder (1)
